# Copy to .env.local (not committed). Vite only exposes VITE_ prefixed variables to the client.
#
# Where the API is lives in .env.development (`npm run dev`: the local server
# on :5000) and .env.production (`npm run build`: https://api.theartistry360.com).
# .env.local wins over both, so keep VITE_API_* and VITE_REALTIME_URL out of it.
# Optional, in either: VITE_API_VERSION (v1), VITE_API_TIMEOUT (15000 ms).

# Sign-in (live): Google and Apple only, the same accounts as voting on
# theartistry360.com. Each button shows only when its id is set. The Google
# web client must list this site's address (http://localhost:5174,
# https://stream.theartistry360.com) under Authorized JavaScript origins, and
# the Apple Services ID must list it under its domains and return URLs.
# In production, set them as Netlify environment variables.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_APPLE_SERVICES_ID=
